// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.58pt, 790.2pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 96.26pt, "Abstract:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 133.46pt, "Laser dynamics underpin a broad range of modern photonic technologies and continue to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 161.06pt, "reveal rich nonlinear behaviors. However, existing spectroscopic tools—most notably ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 188.66pt, "time-stretched dispersive Fourier transform spectroscopy (TS-DFT)—remain limited in ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 216.26pt, "spectral resolution, accuracy, and their ability to capture continuous waveforms and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 243.86pt, "complex field dynamics. Here, we introduce dual-comb correlation spectroscopy (DCCS) ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 271.49pt, "as a powerful approach for resolving fast and intricate laser behaviors that are inaccessible ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 299.09pt, "to TS-DFT and conventional spectrometers. By correlating two sequences of heterodyne ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 326.69pt, "spectra produced by mixing a test laser with a pair of optical combs, DCCS enables rapid ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 354.29pt, "(e.g., 1 µs) and high-resolution (0.08 pm) spectral retrieval over broad optical bandwidths. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 381.89pt, "Leveraging these capabilities, we reveal mode-hopping and mode-competition dynamics ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 409.49pt, "in continuous-wave lasers, as well as the buildup process of a mode-locked laser. These ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 437.11pt, "results establish DCCS as a versatile and complementary tool to TS-DFT for exploring ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 464.71pt, "transient, broadband, and previously unresolvable behaviors in lasers and other time-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 492.43pt, "evolving optical systems. ")
]

