  #line-at(85.104pt, 100.1pt, "Introduction")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 140.78pt, "Understanding the dynamic behavior of lasers, such as noise build-up, mode competition, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 168.38pt, "and pulse formation, is essential for advancing photonic technologies ranging from high-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 195.98pt, "speed communication ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(196.37pt, 195.98pt, "[1]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.41pt, 195.98pt, " to precision metrology ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(331.63pt, 195.98pt, "[2]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(345.67pt, 195.98pt, ". However, conventional Fourier-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 223.58pt, "transform spectrometers and camera-based dispersive spectrometers are too slow to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 251.21pt, "capture these phenomena [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(217.01pt, 251.21pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.01pt, 251.21pt, "]. Under this circumstance, time-stretch dispersive Fourier ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 278.81pt, "transform spectroscopy (TS-DFT) has emerged as a powerful method for probing soliton ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 306.41pt, "dynamics in real time ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(190.97pt, 306.41pt, "[4-6]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(215.09pt, 306.41pt, ". By mapping spectral information into the time domain using ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 334.01pt, "chromatic dispersion, TS-DFT has enabled real-time monitoring of transient phenomena ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 361.61pt, "such as soliton formation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(211.49pt, 361.61pt, "[7]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(225.53pt, 361.61pt, ", optical rogue waves ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(332.83pt, 361.61pt, "[8]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.87pt, 361.61pt, ", and Q-switching instabilities ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(496.3pt, 361.61pt, "[9]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 389.21pt, "in mode-locked lasers. Despite its success, TS-DFT inherently measures only the spectral ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 416.83pt, "intensity of coherent pulses with a limited spectral resolution (e.g., 0.01-1 nm [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(471.22pt, 416.83pt, "10-12")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(499.18pt, 416.83pt, "]), ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 444.43pt, "lacking direct access to phase and frequency-mode information—quantities that are ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 472.03pt, "essential for fully characterizing the complex field evolution of mode-locked and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 499.63pt, "continuous-wave (CW) lasers ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(230.69pt, 499.63pt, "[13, 14]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(268.85pt, 499.63pt, ". ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 541.15pt, "Optical frequency combs, with their precisely spaced and phase-coherent spectral lines, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 568.75pt, "have opened new frontiers in both spectroscopic and temporal resolution ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(431.26pt, 568.75pt, "[15, 16]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.82pt, 568.75pt, ". Among ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 596.38pt, "the most impactful applications is dual-comb spectroscopy (DCS), which leverages the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 623.98pt, "interference between two combs with slightly detuned repetition rates to perform high-")
