  #line-at(96.984pt, 154.34pt, "Finally, we applied DCCS to investigate mode-locked laser dynamics. We constructed ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 181.94pt, "a nonlinear-polarization-rotation (NPR) mode-locked fiber laser (Supplementary Fig. S1), ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 209.54pt, "emitting pulses at a 21.7 MHz repetition rate with an average output power of 3 mW. The ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 237.14pt, "laser output was split into two paths: one (0.5 mW) directed to the TS-DFT system to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 264.77pt, "generate a reference spectrum, and the other (2.5 mW) to the DCCS system for dual-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 292.37pt, "comb heterodyne detection. Optical and electronic delays between the two paths were ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 319.97pt, "pre-calibrated to synchronize the TS-DFT and DCCS measurements.  ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 361.61pt, "Figure 4a shows a representative 2D TS-DFT spectrogram capturing the laser startup ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 389.21pt, "dynamics, i.e., the evolution from a narrowband pulsing state to a broadband mode-locked ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 416.83pt, "state. Broadband mode-locking emerges at an observation time of t=3.1 ms, with a central ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 444.43pt, "wavelength of 1560 nm and first-order Kelly sidebands located at 1547.85 nm and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 472.03pt, "1570.57 nm (Fig. 4b). In particular, we investigated both the transition stage (dashed box ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 499.63pt, "in Fig. 4a) and the subsequent mode-locked state, in which a strong spectral spike—")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 527.23pt, "normally attributed to a quasi-CW component—appears in the steady-state spectrum but ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 554.83pt, "is absent in the TS-DFT measurement (Fig. 4b).  ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 596.38pt, "We plotted the 3D TS-DFT and DCCS spectrograms (spanning 1558.8–1566.74 nm ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 623.98pt, "over a duration exceeding 1 ms) in Figs. 4c and 4d, respectively. The TS-DFT ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 651.58pt, "measurement reveals a narrowband spectral feature at 1562.8 nm (Fig. 4c), indicating the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 679.18pt, "presence of a dominant picosecond pulse [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
