  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(302.35pt, 679.18pt, "]. This agrees with the DCCS spectrogram, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 706.78pt, "which shows a corresponding spectral component at the same wavelength (marked by a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 734.38pt, "white arrow in Fig. 4d). Note that this weak heterodyne signal gradually fades because, ")
]

// arXiv source page 14
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, (image("graphics/page-14.png", width: 428pt), 83.5pt, 85pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.94pt, 790.2pt, "14 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 95.9pt, "as the pulse spectrum broadens, the power per spectral element decreases, leading to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 123.5pt, "smaller heterodyne amplitudes that eventually sink below the noise floor. Nevertheless, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 151.1pt, "we emphasize two relevant findings: (1) a strong CW component at 1561.7 nm (red arrow) ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 178.7pt, "appears in the DCCS measurement but is absent in the TS-DFT results; and (2) the TS-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 206.3pt, "DFT spectral profile of the dominant pulse exhibits an asymmetric shape, as highlighted ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 233.9pt, "by the pink curves within the black dashed boxes in Fig. 4e. We attribute this asymmetric ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 261.53pt, "Fano-like resonance [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(188.09pt, 261.53pt, "31")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(200.09pt, 261.53pt, "] to the interaction between the CW component (blue peak in Fig. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 289.13pt, "4e) and the dominant pulse. Numerical simulations (Supplementary Fig. S4) corroborate ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 316.73pt, "this mechanism and show excellent agreement with the experimental data. ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 358.25pt, "After the laser entered the broadband mode-locked state, the CW component abruptly ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 385.85pt, "dropped (zoom-in view in Fig. 4d) and became spectrally noisy (Fig. 4f). This noisy, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 413.45pt, "unstable signal is the origin of the spike observed by the OSA (in Fig. 4f and Fig. 4b). ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 441.07pt, "This finding is generally consistent with previous studies, which attributed the spike to a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 468.67pt, "quasi-CW component [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(196.13pt, 468.67pt, "32")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(208.01pt, 468.67pt, "]. We note that, in contrast to the OSA data in Fig. 4f—acquired ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 496.27pt, "with a 10 pm (1.2 GHz) resolution—DCCS attains a substantially finer resolution of 0.08 ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 523.87pt, "pm (10 MHz), thereby resolving the spectral structure hidden beneath the envelope. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 569.71pt, "Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96.984pt, 610.42pt, "DCCS offers excellent spectral resolving capability for measuring continuous ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 638.02pt, "waveforms and multi-mode signals, making it a unique and complementary tool to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 665.62pt, "existing techniques, including TS-DFT, for probing fast-evolving laser dynamics. For ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 693.22pt, "example, the dual-comb measurements in Figs. 4d and 4e provide direct evidence of a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 720.82pt, "CW component responsible for the Fano-like spectral profile observed in the TS-DFT ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 748.416pt, "results (Figs. 4c and 4e). ")
]

